{
 "note": "CATALOG ROUTES ROSTER. Read by desks/mt5/research/catalog_routes.py every hour. One row per portal: id, route (ckan | dcat_pod | dcat_jsonld | opendatasoft | sdmx | stac | cdx | keyed | probe), base, country (ISO2, EU, WORLD or a region), region, language, producer, producer_type, optional subnational. Add a portal by adding a row; nothing is hard-coded in the module. NO URL here is probed from the cloud container that wrote it (2026-10-06, no egress): every portal's first pass on the box is its probe, and an unparseable answer reads UNMEASURED, never zero.",
 "boundary": "No crypto-exchange host is ever a portal, a CDX domain or an endpoint (MT5 mandate 2026-08-18). blocked_hosts below is enforced on every request and every endpoint; names without a dot match any host label containing them.",
 "schema_version": 1,
 "defaults": {
  "rows": 100,
  "pages_per_visit": 3,
  "max_entries_per_visit": 400,
  "min_gap_s": 1.0,
  "relist_days": 7,
  "timeout_s": 25,
  "cdx_index": null,
  "cdx_filter_field": "mimetype"
 },
